From: Kuzma30 <kuzemkoa@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 15:14:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 18/24] Modeling Algorithms - Close a fillet ending in the
 plane of the next face

FreeCAD issue 20085, continued: in the cube with fillets of radius 6 and
a square hole of 8 x 8, filleting only some edges of the hole makes the
fillets end at corners of the hole whose next edge is not filleted. The
section at such an end lies in the plane of the next wall of the hole,
and that plane also holds the edge between the fillet of the cube and
the sphere of its corner. The wall must be extended up to the end of the
fillet and bounded by that edge.

ChFi3d_Builder::PerformIntersectionAtEnd did so only when the faces at
the vertex were found from the side of the sphere (the case pro15368 of
a vertex with five edges, two of them tangent: one face cut, the other
reached along the arc). Found from the side of the wall, the fillet was
cut by the wall, the fillet of the cube and the sphere: a patch with a
tolerance of 0.009 to 9 and an invalid sphere. The same case is now
recognized from that side.

Also, the curve along the arc took its ends in the period of its circle
where the vertex was found, not in the range of the edge: on a seam
ending at the period, the curve went around the circle and the pcurve
on the sphere left its domain. The ends are now taken in the range of
the edge, and the shift of periodic curves done after it is skipped for
such a curve.

With the 8 edges of the hole and the subsets tried (each edge alone, two or
three neighbouring edges, opposite edges, upper and lower), the result is
valid with tolerance 1e-4 for r = 0.5 to 2.9 (5.6e-4 at 2.9); the removed
volumes add up (r = 2: 14.18 mm3 per fillet, 1.99 mm3 per corner).

New DRAW test bugs/modalg_8/fillet_rounded_cube_square_hole_ends and GTest
BRepFilletAPI_MakeFilletTest.SquareHoleInRoundedCube_FilletEndsInWallPlane.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01N85duF92anuCHYJzUxLgPg
